Appendix D: Research & Development Roadmap

This appendix outlines key areas of ongoing research and development that will refine the DPS and its components.

D1. ER Fluid for Ball Bladder (TRL 5 → 7)

· Goal: Transition from lab-validated ER fluid to a durable, miniaturised bladder for matchball.
· Challenges: Ensuring consistent performance under temperature variation, impact stresses, and long-term cycling; developing a reliable hermetic seal.
· Timeline: Estimated 2–3 years for a field-ready prototype after targeted materials science R&D.

D2. Predictive Neural Network for Footfall (TRL 4 → 7)

· Goal: Develop a compact, low-latency physics-informed neural network (PINN) for real-time footstrike prediction.
· Challenges: Training on diverse movement patterns (sprinting, shuffling, cutting); ensuring model robustness to sensor noise; achieving inference in <5 ms on an embedded system.
· Timeline: 1–2 years for a field-ready prototype, leveraging current advances in deep learning for time-series prediction.

D3. Wearable Control Moment Gyroscope (IEV) (TRL 5 → 7)

· Goal: Create a lightweight, low-profile CMG suit for stabilising the human torso during high-impact cuts in hypogravity.
· Challenges: Miniaturising CMG gimbals without sacrificing torque; managing gyroscopic precession effects on the wearer; integrating with a predictive control loop.
· Timeline: 3–5 years for a field-ready prototype. The V2Suit project serves as a valuable starting point.

D4. Lava Tube Arena Infrastructure (TRL 2 → 5)

· Goal: Validate the feasibility of converting a lunar or Martian lava tube into a pressurised, sealed arena.
· Challenges: Mapping and characterising tube geology from orbit; developing sealants for porous rock; designing airlock systems; modelling structural stability under pressurisation.
· Timeline: A long-term project (10+ years), contingent on orbital survey data and potential robotic precursor missions.

D5. Long-Term Hypogravity Sensorimotor Adaptation (TRL 4 → 6)

· Goal: Understand and optimise human motor adaptation to hypogravity combined with DPS equipment.
· Challenges: The native skipping gait and altered ball-striking mechanics require targeted training.
· Potential Approach: Leverage the CHAPEA analogues, AlterG treadmills with VR, and the Native Clause in Law 12 to co-evolve technique with technology.

