Appendix E: Glossary of Terms & Acronyms

Term / Acronym Definition
AOS Automated Officiating System. Non-discretionary assistant to the referee for specific violations (e.g., Cadence Drift, Height Violation).
CHAPEA Crew Health and Performance Exploration Analog. NASA's series of analog missions simulating year-long stays on Mars (e.g., 3D-printed "Mars Dune Alpha").
CMG Control Moment Gyroscope. A device using a spinning rotor on a gimbal to produce a torque. Used in the DPS-0 ball for Magnus simulation and in the Inertial Equilibrium Vest for torso stabilisation.
D-Boot Vector Boot. The mandatory player boot with distinct touch and plant zones, hybrid adhesion, and MRE studs.
DPS Dribble Preservation Standard. The core framework and engineering philosophy detailed in the Blueprint.
EA Electroadhesion. An electrically controllable adhesion technology used to augment grip in the D-Boot plant zone.
EPM Electropermanent Magnet. A magnet that can be switched on/off with an electrical pulse, used for zero-hold-power adhesion.
ER Fluid Electrorheological Fluid. A smart fluid whose viscosity can be controlled by an electric field. Used in the DPS-0 ball bladder to adjust restitution.
ERE Electrorheological Elastomer. A solid version of an electrorheological fluid, where the elastomer's stiffness is controlled by an electric field.
FIFA Fédération Internationale de Football Association. The international governing body of association football.
g Acceleration due to gravity. g₀ = Earth (9.81 m s⁻²); g_M = Mars (3.72 m s⁻²); g_L = Moon (1.62 m s⁻²).
Hardware Doping Illegal modification of D-Boot or IEV firmware to produce performance exceeding Earth-equivalent lateral acceleration. Carries severe penalties (Law 4).
H_crit Critical Height. The vertical out-of-bounds boundary set at 4.5 m above the pitch (Law 1).
IEV Inertial Equilibrium Vest. The mandatory wearable torso stabilisation unit with CMGs.
IFAB International Football Association Board. The body that determines the Laws of the Game for association football.
IMU Inertial Measurement Unit. An electronic device measuring acceleration, angular velocity, and magnetic field.
LBPPT Lower-Body Positive Pressure Treadmill. A treadmill that uses air pressure to reduce effective body weight (e.g., AlterG).
LRS Lunar Radar Sounder. A radar instrument onboard the JAXA SELENE (Kaguya) lunar orbiter, used to detect subsurface lava tubes.
Magnus Effect The phenomenon where a spinning object (e.g., a football) curves in flight. The DPS-0 ball emulates this using a CMG in hypogravity.
MRE Magnetorheological Elastomer. A smart material whose stiffness is controlled by a magnetic field. Used in the pitch surface and D-Boot studs.
MRF Magnetorheological Fluid. A smart fluid whose viscosity is controlled by a magnetic field.
Native Clause Law 12, Section E. Protects the evolved dribbling styles (e.g., skip-dribble) of players born or long-term resident in hypogravity.
PINN Physics-Informed Neural Network. A neural network that incorporates physical laws into its training, used here for predictive foot placement.
PTP Precision Time Protocol (IEEE 802.1AS). A protocol for clock synchronisation across a network.
SAOT Semi-Automated Offside Technology. System used by FIFA, combined with Connected Ball Technology to enhance offside decisions.
SELENE (Kaguya) Japanese lunar orbiter mission (2007-2009) that provided high-resolution imagery and radar data for lava tube discovery.
TRL Technology Readiness Level. A scale from 1 (basic principles) to 9 (proven in operational environment) to measure technological maturity.
UWB Ultra-Wideband. A radio technology used for precise real-time localisation, used in boots and pitch grid for foot placement tracking.
VAR Video Assistant Referee. The system used in professional football to assist on-field referees using video footage.
VIFK Vertical Indirect Free Kick. A restart for crossing H_crit, taken at ground level (Law 1).
V2Suit Variable Vector Countermeasure Suit. A NASA research suit with CMGs for astronaut stabilisation, a precursor to the IEV.


